  "idea": "How to summarize long YouTube videos in 10 seconds without watching them",
  "text": "Never sit through a 45-minute YouTube video just to get one answer again. Searching for quick answers in long tutorials usually means scrubbing through sponsor breaks and creator banter. Scrubbing blindly wastes study time and leaves you missing the exact steps you need. Instead, use a free Chrome extension like Glasp or Eightify to convert video transcripts into concise bullet points. You pull key insights in ten seconds.",
